    "uncertain_handling": {
      "_comment": "NLP-derived multi-label, no per-label uncertainty marker (unlike CheXpert's -1). NaN Labels rows (103 of 160,861) are always dropped. Image-level uncertainty is expressed via two meta-labels — 'exclude' (1,312 rows) and 'suboptimal_study' (1,839 rows, ~3,151 combined). With the harmonizer's default drop_uncertain=True these rows are also dropped, leaving 157,607 rows; pass drop_uncertain=False to keep the full noisy distribution (160,758 rows).",
